    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The lead program, darovasertib, achieved a pivotal milestone: its Phase 2/3 registrational trial in first-line metastatic uveal melanoma met the primary endpoint, positioning IDEAYA to address a high unmet need in a niche oncology setting. Broader pipeline momentum is building, with multiple clinical updates expected in the second half of the year across neoadjuvant uveal melanoma, DLL3-targeting ADCs, and MTAP-deleted cancer programs. The precision oncology landscape remains competitive, but successful data readouts are strengthening the company’s commercial and clinical footing.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is translating positive registrational data into near-term regulatory action, initiating a Real-Time Oncology Review submission and targeting NDA filing later this year. The team is actively refining the pipeline, discontinuing certain combination studies to concentrate resources on higher-conviction assets like IDE849 and the PRMT5/MAT2A pair. With a robust cash position and disciplined capital allocation, management is advancing multiple programs toward registrational trials while maintaining a well-funded runway, reinforcing credibility with investors after de-risking the lead asset.",
